invariant: INV-13
file: tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: the tcp-nonblocking client stages no alert record when its handshake
  fails, so ch_record_out answers CH_EINVAL at once and the caller, who holds
  no key, has nothing to send the server before it closes.
  bin/tcp_nonblocking_loop_test requires ch_record_out to hand over each
  failure's alert record once, which the server then reads.

--- old
    memcpy(r->t.tx, rec, rec_len);
    r->tx_len = rec_len;
--- new
    memcpy(r->t.tx, rec, rec_len);
